# A Nova D1 app: one text file in /nova/apps. No rebuild, no package, no reboot.
# Only app.name is required. Keep the header near the top — the home screen
# reads the first 512 bytes of each file to build the catalogue.

app.name:     Device Check
app.ver:      1.0.0
app.dev:      dash1101
# Wireless, Sensors, Tools, System or Testing. Default is Tools.
app.category: System
app.desc:     Four questions worth asking a board that is behaving oddly.
app.kind:     rows

Tasks       = ps
Storage     = df
Memory      = free
Packages    = pkg list

# A row is "Label = command". The command is an ordinary shell line — whatever
# you would type over serial — and its output lands in a scrollable pane. The
# label stops at the FIRST '=', so the rest of the line is all command.
#
# You can call the FIRMWARE commands: cc1101, sx1276, bt, nfc, ibutton, net,
# fetch, ping, reg, pkg, script, sd, ls, cat, ps, df, free, service.
#
# You cannot call the PACKAGED ones: gpio, i2cscan, dht, ws2812, calc. A Nova D1
# screen is already inside Nova D1's sandbox and the OS allows one package call
# per task, so it refuses a second. The same line works typed at the console,
# because a console is not inside a package — that catches people out, and it is
# not a bug in your app.
#
# Anything with a loop or a condition in it belongs in a script:
#
#   Sweep = script /nova/scripts/sweep.rps
